# OHM bundles are canonical UTF-8 byte streams (docs/adr/0003-ohm-yaml.md
# "Contrato de preservacao"; backend/oharness/codec.py). CRLF-preserving
# authored content is encoded as double-quoted \r\n escapes specifically so
# raw CR/LF bytes never appear inside these files -- but this repo's
# core.autocrlf=true would still rewrite each file's own *structural* LF
# line breaks to CRLF on a Windows checkout, changing the bytes actually on
# disk (decode() recovers the same value either way, but the file would no
# longer match what encode() produced, and codec.py's "second export is
# byte-identical" guarantee would look violated when compared against a
# freshly checked-out copy). `-text` disables that normalization.
backend/oharness/fixtures/*.ohm -text
backend/oharness/fixtures/*.legacy.json -text
tests/fixtures/ohm/**/*.yaml -text
tests/fixtures/ohm/*.ohm -text
tests/fixtures/ohm/*.json -text

# The permission mode table is shipped twice and a test compares the bytes; keep LF on every checkout.
backend/sandbox/permission_modes.json text eol=lf
frontend/src/lib/permissionModes.json text eol=lf
